## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical PIM/JIT implementation with governance.

## Key Concepts
- Privileged Identity Management (PIM)
- Just-In-Time (JIT) access
- Activation workflow and MFA
- Approvals, auditing, and alerts
- Emergency break-glass handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// PIM-like activation flow (illustrative)
const activate = async (roleId, user) => {
  // request activation with approval
  await graphClient.post(`/roleAssignments`, { roleDefinitionId: roleId, principalId: user });
  // MFA enforcement occurs at login/activation
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the emergency bypass path and ensure controls aren’t bypassed?
- How would you export and present an audit report of activations for compliance?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical app registration for a mobile app using PKCE with Azure AD, focusing on public client setup, permissions, and cleanup.

## Key Concepts

- Public client app registration
- Redirect URIs for mobile apps
- API permissions and consent
- PKCE flow basics
- Token validation and cleanup

## Code Example

```javascript
// MSAL config for a mobile app
const msalConfig = {
  auth: {
    clientId: "YOUR_CLIENT_ID",
    authority: "https://login.microsoftonline.com/YOUR_TENANT_ID",
    redirectUri: "com.example.app://auth"
  },
  cache: { cacheLocation: "localStorage" }
};
const loginRequest = { scopes: ["User.Read"] };
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this for multi-tenant access?
- What changes if the app transitions to a confidential client?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a beginner's grasp of Conditional Access basics and practical gating for real-world apps.

## Key Concepts
- Conditional Access
- Location and device-based access
- Intune device compliance
- Sandbox validation and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Illustrative CA policy snippet (formatting for clarity)
{
  "applications": {"include": ["https://contoso-app" ]},
  "conditions": {
    "locations": {"include": ["trusted"]},
    "devices": {"include": ["compliant"]},
    "users": {"include": ["AllUsers"]}
  },
  "grant": {"operator": "OR", "builtInControls": ["mfa"]}
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this policy using a sandbox user and what logs would you inspect?
- What are common pitfalls when combining location-based and device-based CA policies?
